<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Maven settings for the verification agent. Pass with `-s`, or point BBC_MVN_SETTINGS at it.

  WHY THIS FILE EXISTS. The user-level ~/.m2/settings.xml carries a `<mirrorOf>*</mirrorOf>`
  mirror, added for a different project to route around a defunct repository
  (maven.restlet.com, which had begun serving an HTML landing page that Maven cached as
  corrupt jars). `*` mirrors EVERY repository, including the ones a client legitimately
  declares for itself, so a client whose dependencies are not all on Central cannot resolve
  at all under it.

  That produced a SILENT false negative, which is the dangerous kind. onthegomap/planetiler
  needs org.geotools from the OSGeo repository it declares in its own POM; under the global
  mirror those requests went to Central, 404'd, and the version knob probe reported "build
  resolved None". In the ledger that is indistinguishable from "this client does not depend
  on the library", so the candidate would have been written off as unverifiable for a reason
  that has nothing to do with the client, the library, or the break.

  So: mirror Central only. A client's own repositories are left alone, which is the point.

  (Note for editors: XML comments may not contain a double hyphen. An earlier revision of
  this header used them as dashes and made the file non-parseable, which Maven reports as
  "Error executing Maven / problem building the effective settings" on every goal, while
  `mvn -version` still succeeds because it never reads settings.)
-->
<settings xmlns="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0"
          xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
          xsi:schemaLocation="http://maven.apache.org/SETTINGS/1.0.0 https://maven.apache.org/xsd/settings-1.0.0.xsd">
  <mirrors>
    <mirror>
      <id>central-mirror</id>
      <name>Central only, never a client's own repositories</name>
      <url>https://repo1.maven.org/maven2</url>
      <mirrorOf>central</mirrorOf>
    </mirror>
  </mirrors>
</settings>
